  {
   "type": "text",
   "title": "What this is",
   "gridPos": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "w": 24,
    "h": 3
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "content": "Names that **resemble** a Korean bank, courier or telecom brand and have a TLS certificate. Resemblance is all it means: a name here may be the brand's own, a partner, a defensive registration or a squatter. Nothing is ever resolved, fetched or visited \u2014 the only source is the public Certificate Transparency index.\n\nCandidates are **generated**, not searched for, so this finds only impersonations the generator imagined. See `docs/limits.md`."
   }
  },
